.venv

# generated by the QA gate, the legacy wrapper and the crawl
output/qa/
output/contract_legacy/
plan/logs/
plan/catalog.tsv.partial

# GPU batch staging: manifests, pulled transcripts (QA FAILs stay here), pod logs
output/batches/

# segmentation probes: captions, info.json, section clips (pipeline/segment.py)
output/segtest/

# T0 probes (plan/T0-TESTPLAN.md): captions, info.json, section clips, classifier output
output/t0/

# T2 run artefacts (plan/T2-PLAN.md 3a-3d): stage logs, the ASR wavs / VTTs / reports
output/t2/
output/validation/

# name-redaction pass (pipeline/redact.py, DECISIONS #15): redacted transcripts are
# regenerable output; the audit/review CSVs hold the ORIGINAL names for the hand
# check and must never be committed. CALIBRATION.md was the one tracked exception
# until 2026-10-20 — it is a working note on how the redactor was tuned, it quotes
# its calibration set, and no page links it, so it now stays on disk and out of the
# repo like the rest of this directory. The whole directory stays ignored.
output/redacted/*
.env*

# Every pilot and wave now writes its own output/<name>/ subdir (CSV/JSON/PNG
# tables, run logs), and output/fullasr/audio/ holds whole-meeting audio — one
# FLAC there is 770 MB. Listing them one at a time has not kept up, so ignore
# the whole tree; output/redacted/ keeps its own rules above.
output/*
!output/redacted/

# scratch run logs from the one-off scripts (make test, swagit probes, R installs)
logs/

# Session hand-off notes under docs/. They are working notes to the next operator —
# what was in flight, which batch to watch, what to pick up — not documentation of
# the study, and docs/ is the published GitHub Pages root. Untracked 2026-10-20;
# they stay on disk.
docs/RESUME.md
docs/RESUME-BRIEF.md
# Same category: the incident note for the lowercase-name leak that redact-1.2 fixes.
# It is the operator's record — what leaked, where, what the old residual scan could
# not see, and the editorial numbers that went stale with it — and pipeline/redact.py
# cites it for the reasoning behind the ci_ layers. Owner's call whether it is ever
# published; until then it stays on disk and out of the Pages root.
docs/REDACTION-LEAK-2026-10-20.md
